  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Soran Singh And Others vs State Of U.P. And Another on 20 November, 2023 Author: Neeraj Tiwari Bench: Neeraj Tiwari High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ? Neutral Citation No. - 2023:Ahc:219781 Court No. - 87 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 4054 of 2011 Applicant :- Soran Singh And Others Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Another Counsel for Applicant :- Babban Singh Rathore,Ramesh Chandra Pandey Counsel for Opposite Party :- Govt.Advocate, Hon'ble Neeraj Tiwari,J. 1. 3. It is submitted that an FIR has been lodged against the applicants under Sections 272, 273 I.P.C. Thereafter, a parallel proceeding arising out of same offence has also been initiated before Judicial Magistrate-I, Fatehabad, Agra, which was registered as Case No. 1816 of 2010, under Section 7/16 The Prevention of Food Adulteration Act.",
    "facts": "3. It is submitted that an FIR has been lodged against the applicants under Sections 272, 273 I.P.C. Thereafter, a parallel proceeding arising out of same offence has also been initiated before Judicial Magistrate-I, Fatehabad, Agra, which was registered as Case No. 1816 of 2010, under Section 7/16 The Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. He next submitted that in the said proceeding, applicants Soran Singh And Others vs State Of U.P. And Another on 20 November, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199056532/ 1 have moved discharge application, which was allowed vide order dated 4.3.2016. 4. He has also brought the facts on record by filing supplementary affidavit dated 22.08.2023. In para 4 of the supplementary affidavit, it is clearly averred that they have been discharged by the lower court, vide order dated 04.03.2016, which is part of supplementary affidavit.",
    "arguments": "It is next submitted that once the applicants have been discharged in parallel proceeding, the present proceedings is bad in law and and is liable to [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 5. Learned AGA has also filed supplementary counter affidavit dated 2.9.2023 to the supplementary affidavit dated 22.8.2023. In the supplementary counter affidavit filed by the State, there is no denial of facts as argued by the learned counsel for the applicants. 6. Even today before the Court, learned AGA could not demonstrate from the records and from the supplementary counter affidavit filed by the State against the arguments made by the learned counsel for the applicants.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is next submitted that once the applicants have been discharged in parallel proceeding, the present proceedings is bad in law and and is liable to [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 5. Learned AGA has also filed supplementary counter affidavit dated 2.9.2023 to the supplementary affidavit dated 22.8.2023. In the supplementary counter affidavit filed by the State, there is no denial of facts as argued by the learned counsel for the applicants. 6. Even today before the Court, learned AGA could not demonstrate from the records and from the supplementary counter affidavit filed by the State against the arguments made by the learned counsel for the applicants.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
